\title{Remarks on extension by linearity}
\taxon{Remark}
\date{2022-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\ul{
\li{This is true in the infinite dimensional case as well.}
\li{Often, to define a linear map, we define its value on a basis and “extend by linearity”.}
\li{If #{\alpha_1, \alpha_2 \colon V \to W} are linear and agree on a basis of #{V}, they are equal.}
}
